    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • Skoda Joins the Party at the 2026 Paris Motor Show With New Epiq Sportline Model, Here's the Price\nVolkswagen, Audi, and Porsche All Lost US Sales in Q3 2026\n19 photos\nPhoto: Volkswagen of America\nThe Volkswagen Group's core brands in the United States market had a rough third quarter. For starters, Volkswagen sold 11,481 fewer ID.4 electric crossovers than a year earlier. Its collapse helps explain why the internal combustion Tiguan and Jetta could not prevent an overall decline, while Audi and Porsche faced their own problems with electric vehicles and product transitions.\nAltogether, these brands reported 133,956 deliveries in the third quarter of 2026 stateside. Compared to 152,866 in the third quarter of 2025, that's down 12.4 percent. Volkswagen's total fell 10.9 percent to 78,179 units, Audi deliveries contracted 15 percent to 39,751 vehicles, and Porsche dropped 12.9 percent to 16,026 deliveries in the United States of America.\nAs noted earlier, the gas-powered Tiguan and Jetta provided some relief for the corest of Volkswagen Group brands. Tiguan sales improved 27.4 percent to 28,091 units, making it the best-selling Volkswagen of the quarter. Jetta sales rose 24.9 percent to 14,092 units, while the Taos crossover held flat at 9,780 deliveries. Those increases lifted passenger car sales 16.6 percent.\nThe SUV line had it worse, for combined sales of the Atlas and ID. models fell sharply enough to drag total sport utility vehicle volume down 16.2 percent. Atlas fell 19.5 percent, Atlas Cross Sport slipped 9.5 percent, and the ID.4 recorded a pitiful 989 deliveries compared to an even worse 432 for the ID. Buzz family hauler.\nThere is, however, some context at play here. Federal tax credits are no longer a thing, and the ID.4 is no longer available to configure stateside. Production came to a screeching halt earlier this year, freeing valuable Chattanooga plant output for the redesigned Atlas and Atlas Cross Sport. The existing ID.4 inventory could last into 2027.\nPhoto: Porsche There is a planned future version of the ID.4 for North America, and that vehicle is called the ID. Tiguan. With a bit of luck, the newcomer should hit dealer lots in the latter half of 2027 as a 2028 model. Audi 's story is a bit more complicated, with the premium-oriented automaker from Ingolstadt delivering 39,751 vehicles in the past quarter.\nSeveral recently introduced models gained ground, of which the A5 stands out for improving 53 percent. A6 volume rose 36 percent, Q3 sales 24 percent, and the Q5 improved by 17 percent. While it may be pricier, the Q7 advanced 42 percent to 6,071 units. The aging Q8, meanwhile, more than doubled sales to 4,095 units.\nSaid gains weren't enough to cover falling Q6 e-tron deliveries, and it's really bad. The Premium Platform Electric-based model nosedived from 10,059 units to 619 last quarter, whereas the Q4 e-tron dropped from 2,956 to 8 examples of the breed. The A6 Sportback e-tron, which uses similar underpinnings to the Q6 e-tron, also slid a lot. Of course, e-tron GT sales fell as well.\nPorsche's decline is noteworthy as well, a decline attributed by the Zuffenhausen-based marque to the lower volume of 718 sales. Both gas-powered models are on their way out for good to make room for the 718 Electric line, and yes, Porsche is not bringing the gas-powered 718 back. Instead, the full-electric version will have to suffice from 2027 forward.\nOf the 16,026 vehicles Porsche dealers moved in the US in Q3 2026, the Cayenne was the biggest winner, contributing 5,837 sales compared to 5,519 for the Macan. The internal combustion 718, by comparison, sold 8 units. The Taycan, which is clearly showing its age, didn't fare well. Instead of 1,553 deliveries in Q3 2025, it fell to 537 this past quarter.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nVolkswagen Audi Porsche sales US industry\nDownload: VW, Audi, Porsche Q3 2026 US sales releases (PDF)\nAbout the author: Mircea Panait\nAfter a 1:43 scale model of a Ferrari 250 GTO sparked Mircea's interest for cars when he was a kid, an early internship at Top Gear sealed his career path. He's most interested in muscle cars and American trucks, but he takes a passing interest in quirky kei cars as well. Full profile\nUP NEXT 5 Innovative Cars You Didn't Know Are the Vision of a Single Individual",
